data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":329,"item_id":"fc_0aa41dd63d0397f1016adb47c48da48191927841174278e096","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"TASK_INCOMPLETE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"R001/S001-S002 source closure and source/application accounting\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"I inspected selected-model-measure-bridge.json, the frozen outstanding review, and the existing full proof in prior-candidate.json. The existing five M sources are M001-M005, and the proof remains the single full R001 with S001-S003. I reprobed the exact Hausdorff formula under its actual namespace: MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure_apply in Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Hausdorff. Its complete signature is bound in probe result M008 and explicitly gives the supremum over positive scales, infimum over Nat-indexed covers satisfying covering and ediam bounds, and the tsum with nonempty-witness supremum. This corrects the invalid abbreviated global name. I also successfully probed MeasureTheory.lintegral_mono (M009) and MeasureTheory.lintegral_indicator_const (M010); the latter computes an indicator integral as constant times measure, not the interval-length fact itself. A query for MeasureTheory.Measure.real returned a non-theorem and was correctly rejected, so it will not be misrepresented as an M theorem. Source closure and the necessary actual applications/citations have not yet been integrated into the graph; further substantive facts include restricted interval mass/length, finite ambient dimension and zero/infinite-measure dimension consequences, plus all relevant local conditions and exponent coercions. No unsupported mathematical implication is being asserted as a gap; this is unfinished source registration and drafting, so work must continue before submission.\\\"}\"}"}

